{"file_path":"/home/john/mynotes/deterministic_equidistribution_theory/defect_cocycle_with_findings.tex","new_string":"\\begin{remark}[The uniform gap is governed by the \\emph{worst} character]\nA uniform gap means $\\rho(\\Lcal_\\chi)\\le(1-\\kappa_Q)\\rho(\\Lcal_0)$ for\n\\emph{all} $\\chi\\ne1$, so\n$\\kappa_Q=1-\\max_\\chi[\\rho(\\Lcal_\\chi)/\\rho(\\Lcal_{\\chi_0})]$---the\n\\emph{worst}-gapped character. (Computed over the full group via the conjugate\nsymmetry $k=1..\\lfloor\\phi/2\\rfloor$.)\n\\end{remark}\n\n\\begin{findingbox}{Target 1 (the finiteness leak), full character group}\n\\textbf{Killed-height: no uniform gap.} For Q $\\in\\{9,27,81\\}$ the maximum gap\nratio is \\emph{exactly} $1$, at the \\textbf{quadratic character} $k=\\phi/2$:\nthere $\\rho(\\Lcal_\\chi)=\\rho(\\Lcal_{\\chi_0})$ to machine precision---the\nresidue-independent height-transport survival eigenvalue ($0.9119$ at $s{=}0$,\nidentical for every $Q$). So $\\kappa_Q=0$: the height coordinate, appended\nuncoupled from the character, leaves a mode alive in the quadratic sector\n(a construction artifact, residuals $\\sim\\!0$).\n\n\\textbf{Residue-only (the object that governs $W$): a uniform gap survives.}\n$\\kappa_Q=1-\\max_\\chi$ ratio \\emph{stabilizes} as $Q$ grows---$0.236$ at\n$s{=}0$, $0.074$ at $s{=}1$ for all $Q\\in\\{27,\\dots,2187\\}$---bounded well away\nfrom $0$, with the worst character at a \\emph{fixed} frequency, not $k=1$. The\nlowest-frequency $k{=}1$ char, where the annealed $1-\\lvert\\hat p(1/\\phi)\\rvert$\ncollapses to $0$ ($0.42\\to2\\times10^{-5}$ as $Q\\to2187$), is gapped by the\n\\emph{exact} operator by $0.24$--$0.78$: the exact operator gaps low frequencies\n\\emph{far more} than the i.i.d.\\ shadow. The annealed finiteness leak is\n\\textbf{refuted} for the residue operator over $3^2\\to3^7$.\n\\end{findingbox}","old_string":"\\begin{findingbox}{Target 1 (the finiteness leak), on the converged solver}\nWith Arnoldi, the killed-height gap\n$\\kappa_Q=1-\\min_\\chi[\\rho(\\Lcal_\\chi)/\\rho(\\Lcal_{\\chi_0})]$ (minimum over the\nfirst four multiplicative characters) is \\emph{tilt-independent} (the earlier\n$s$-dependence was non-convergence) and \\emph{grows} with $Q$:\n\\[\n\\kappa_9=0.093,\\quad \\kappa_{27}=0.190,\\quad \\kappa_{81}=0.306,\\quad\n\\kappa_{243}=0.329 .\n\\]\nOver the tested range the gap is bounded well away from $0$ and increasing---the\ndirection the uniform-gap hypothesis $\\kappa_Q\\gtrsim 1/\\mathrm{polylog}(Q)$\nrequires. (Caveat: minimum over four characters, not all $\\phi-1$; the\nfiniteness leak as $Q\\to\\infty$ is not settled.)\n\\end{findingbox}","replace_all":false}